WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.160
- In two days, I'm gonna be
hiking The Trans-Catalina Trail.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.200
I'm running around trying
to get last minute supplies.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.428
I'm excited for my trip, but
I'm also feeling very anxious

00:00:10.428 --> 00:00:13.803
because this is my first
serious backpacking trip.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.730
I've had a hard time this past year

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.184
with some things in my personal life

00:00:17.184 --> 00:00:20.413
and also with the death of my
grandpa, who I was close with,

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.640
so I'm doing this hike in
hopes of clearing my mind

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.173
and letting go of some things.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.925
I'm also trying to do this zero waste.

00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:29.764
So, I'm gonna be packing all my food

00:00:29.764 --> 00:00:33.060
as much as possible zero waste.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.750
Zero waste means trying to send

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.773
as little as possible to landfill.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.060
I did this a little last minute,

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.163
and I had no gear to begin with.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.650
So, I ended up spending $459.07.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.370
Backpacking is very expensive,

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:48.750
which is maybe why it's
taken me so long to try it.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.573
I spent $28.83 on all of this food,

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:55.460
and it's gonna last me
for three and a half days.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.580
These are my toiletries, and look,

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.133
I was able to shove it
in this other tiny tin.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.011
I'm feeling very nervous.

00:01:02.011 --> 00:01:05.323
My heart is (gasps) in my chest right now.

00:01:05.557 --> 00:01:07.923
I'm really worried about the weight.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.300
So, this is my pack.

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.800
I'm gonna attempt to put
it on for the first time.

00:01:19.056 --> 00:01:19.889
Alright.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:22.083
I'm gonna tip over.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.860
As women, we're constantly
told that, you know,

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.690
we can't do (bleep)
alone, and you know what?

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.833
We can, we can do things
alone, and watch me.

00:01:35.330 --> 00:01:37.180
- Yeah, because you love being alone.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.640
This is like your idea
of the best time ever.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.333
- [Ari] I'll meet people.

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:44.023
- Will you?

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.743
- I woke up before my alarm.

00:01:46.975 --> 00:01:48.225
I'm very ready.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.100
I'm taking a ferry to Catalina Island,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:53.853
where I'll be hiking along
The Trans-Catalina Trail.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.390
The trail's around 38 miles long,

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.203
and it'll take me about three
and a half days to finish.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.133
I'm here,

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.180
and I'm going to the visitor's
center to get my map.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:07.830
I'm gonna be taking a shuttle
from Avalon to Haypress

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.280
to shave a few miles off of my first day

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:14.330
because I am an inexperienced backpacker.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:15.563
There's a bison.

00:02:17.324 --> 00:02:18.493
Oh my goodness.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.233
I'm ready to start.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.403
I'm so excited!

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:25.700
I don't really know how
many miles I need to go

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.933
or how long it's gonna be.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.593
I'm going to Black Jack Campground.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:34.603
It appears like I'm starting on mile six.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.603
Pretty sure I heard a rattlesnake.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.443
It's nice out here.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:40.603
The pack's very heavy.

00:02:40.771 --> 00:02:42.603
What'd I get myself into?

00:02:42.613 --> 00:02:45.723
Woo hoo, I've done two miles,

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.073
which means I've hardly done anything,

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.281
but I still feel good about it.

00:02:50.281 --> 00:02:53.203
(exhales heavily) These hills are no joke.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:54.623
Look at these views.

00:02:55.843 --> 00:02:57.653
Oh, it's so pretty here.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:02:59.410
I'm gonna stop for lunch.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.510
You have to pack out all of your trash,

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.943
so I have salvaged this plastic bag,

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:07.440
and I'm gonna be putting
all my trash in there.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.463
I'm drenched in sweat,
but I'm staying hydrated.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.950
I don't know how much longer I have to go.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:17.480
I should've paid better
attention to the new map.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.003
I think I might be
already at the campsite.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:22.743
I see some picnic tables.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:25.480
So, it took me three hours and 20 minutes

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.813
to hike from Haypress to Black Jack.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.333
I don't know if I made
good time or bad time.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.760
I'm surprised at how early
I got here, it's only 3:30.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.323
I guess I'll set up my tent and hang out.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.910
This is some curry lentil soup.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:45.213
It's pretty tasty.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:46.993
Day one is over.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:51.280
I spent half of the day
being really excited

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.650
and the other half wondering

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.930
why I would ever do
something like this (laughs).

00:03:56.930 --> 00:04:00.373
I made a new friend, I
hung out by the fire.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.890
So, tomorrow, I'm gonna
be hiking from Black Jack

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:08.403
to Two Harbors, and that's
about 12 to 13 miles.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:10.633
Day two has begun.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.593
It's raining a little bit, but not so bad.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.523
I had my tea, I went
number two, I'm ready.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.893
Yas, mist, yas.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.253
Can you believe this cactus?

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.763
Look at it, look how good it looks.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.313
I've come upon a road, and I
think I'm going the right way.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.413
I looked at the map,
but I'm not really sure.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:34.543
I love snacks.

00:04:35.677 --> 00:04:37.990
I think this is my ideal climate.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:41.843
No chance of sunburn, just
a nice, hydrating mist.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.563
I think I went a minute
or two the wrong way.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.303
I'm lost, and I keep getting more lost,

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.763
and it turns out I'm
a mediocre map reader.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.963
Oh, more signs.

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:56.023
Oh, I finally got back on the track.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.310
I have six miles to Little Harbor,

00:04:58.310 --> 00:04:59.510
which is where I'll have lunch.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:02.453
I got tired, I'm taking
just a little break.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.530
My back is really starting to hurt,

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:14.173
particularly my left shoulder.

00:05:15.873 --> 00:05:19.367
Oh my God, that's so much
weight on my feet with this mud.

00:05:20.366 --> 00:05:22.973
Oh, look, it's the ocean.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.853
I walked from coast to coast.

00:05:26.397 --> 00:05:27.910
(exhales) I'm at Little Harbor.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.073
I found a dry bench to sit on.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.853
I'm eating some leftover oats
from breakfast for lunch.

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:38.610
I have five or so more miles
to go to get to Two Harbors

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.840
where I'll be camping tonight,
and I'm a little worried

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.480
that I lost some time getting lost earlier

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.430
and that I'm not gonna
make it by nightfall.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.970
I refilled my water sack,

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:49.170
but not looking forward
to the extra weight.

00:05:50.899 --> 00:05:53.693
I feel like a hobbit on a long journey,

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:55.667
except I don't have a Mordor.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.103
What up, ravens?

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.063
Slow and steady up this hill.

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:06.303
I'm wet, but my feet aren't,
and that's important.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:10.750
I need a Will Smith inspirational
Twitter video or something

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.923
because I'm ready to
not be walking on hills.

00:06:14.121 --> 00:06:16.623
I didn't even know you
could get this muddy.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:22.053
I think I see the town up ahead.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:25.373
It's really raining and I'm struggling.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.620
So close, but yet so far.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.863
Oh, I finally made it.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.293
I'm cooking in the vestibule of my tent,

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:34.770
maybe it's a fire hazard.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.130
I am the luckiest girl.

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:39.683
I am eating hot soup,
and I am out of the rain.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.140
Don't anyone tell me that this isn't

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:44.363
the most delicious meal, okay?

00:06:44.536 --> 00:06:46.536
(sighs)

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.793
I just lied down for the
first time, and oh my God,

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:56.450
my feet hurt and my
body, but it's a good...

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.203
It just feels good to lay down.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:03.563
I had a pretty good sleep,
I could hear the ocean.

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:06.763
I'm really happy it's
not raining this morning.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:10.523
Everything is so damp still,
so I'm hoping it'll dry off.

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:11.843
Yay, sun!

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:15.010
This is a little solar
charger I'm keeping on my pack

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:16.643
so I can charge my cameras.

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:18.193
There's a little fox.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:20.193
Hi, little fox.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.363
I have just put on my pack,

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:26.673
my shoulders are really
sore from yesterday.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:27.940
My knee started to hurt,

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:29.720
but I think it just needs to warm up.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.860
I gotta go to the visitor's
center and pick up a key

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.033
to get firewood and water
when I'm at Parson's Landing.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:37.093
I got lost.

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:40.333
Apparently I love walking up
hills I don't need to walk up.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.860
God dammit, I went the wrong way again.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.930
I think I'm just really
fatigued this morning,

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:46.563
so I keep making mistakes.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:48.383
So, I gotta watch out for that.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:51.540
It looks like that's where
actually the trail starts.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:53.253
Okay, I'm back on track.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.883
So, I was originally gonna go
from Two Harbors up this way,

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.000
but the visitor's center recommended

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.625
that I just go from here along the coast

00:08:01.625 --> 00:08:04.543
because it's gonna be too
muddy in the interior.

00:08:04.775 --> 00:08:08.123
It's not the true Trans-Catalina trail,

00:08:08.600 --> 00:08:10.163
but I'm okay with that.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:11.693
With every step,

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:15.943
I was having a sharp jolt
of pain in my right knee.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:17.750
So, first, I was mad at my knee,

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:21.560
but then I decided to
thank it and send it love,

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:23.260
and then I remembered this thing

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.295
that my grandma told me once,

00:08:24.295 --> 00:08:29.295
which is that my right foot
bows out a bit when I walk.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.010
So, then I tried to focus

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:37.393
on keeping my feet walking straight,

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.483
and it kind of feels like
writing with your left hand,

00:08:40.624 --> 00:08:43.753
but my knee does not hurt anymore.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:46.283
I'm really learning to listen to my body,

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:50.443
and when my body's in pain,
instead of getting angry it,

00:08:50.787 --> 00:08:52.290
I'm trying to listen

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.370
because it's trying to tell me something,

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.843
and then sort of figure out what I can do.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.603
These views are just murdering my heart.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.083
I'm just so grateful for this beauty,

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:08.263
and it just makes me wanna protect it,

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.580
and I know I could've done better

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:13.250
with my sustainable and no trash efforts,

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:14.590
but I'm happy I tried.

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:17.513
Imma get a tattoo that says sardine queen.

00:09:18.125 --> 00:09:19.673
Oh, these feet hurt.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.553
I think I'm in the final
stretch to Parson's.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:24.363
There's a lot of mud,

00:09:24.558 --> 00:09:28.273
and there's a big ole hill
that I have to get up,

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.113
and it's kind of triggering
my knee stuff again,

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:33.723
but as long as I keep my foot straight,

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:35.833
it doesn't hurt really.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:38.870
My knee does not like going downhill,

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.723
so just taking it really slow.

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:45.020
I'm like 10 feet away from
the campsite, but I just...

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.120
I had to take a break.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:49.463
Hi, John.
- Hi, Ari.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:51.633
Welcome to Parson's Landing.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.010
- [Ari] I think this
is my favorite campsite

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:58.040
because liquid mother is right there.

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.720
So, those are your alcohol
swabs from work, right?

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.813
- Yeah, they taught me how to
make fire in nursing school.

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.500
- [Ari] What's that stick again?

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.513
- It's a ferrocerium rod.

00:10:16.618 --> 00:10:17.618
- [Ari] Wow.

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:23.590
- What did the dad buffalo
say to the son buffalo

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:25.773
when he went to school?
- What?

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:26.980
- He said bye, son.

00:10:27.865 --> 00:10:31.260
- What? (laughs)

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:35.503
I'm cozy in my tent, and I
can hear the ocean waves.

00:10:43.586 --> 00:10:45.800
(yawns) It's the last day.

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:48.270
This was the most fuel efficient
stove I was able to find,

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:50.310
and I'm hoping I can get
a better recommendation.

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:55.113
I have this whole beach to
myself, and I'm enjoying my tea.

00:10:55.310 --> 00:10:56.340
It's 9:30,

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.819
and I just have seven more
miles back to Two Harbors,

00:10:58.819 --> 00:11:00.853
and then the ferry home to L.A.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:03.170
Eating trail mix for
breakfast this morning.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:05.973
It's another beautiful misty day.

00:11:06.270 --> 00:11:08.570
The cool thing about
doing this alone was that

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:11.113
I was able to completely set my own pace.

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:14.223
Mile 35, three more miles to go.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:15.713
Can you hear the sea lions?

00:11:15.918 --> 00:11:17.700
(barking)

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:19.973
Last mile, mile 38!

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:21.833
I did it.

00:11:21.858 --> 00:11:23.080
(screaming)

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:26.283
I kind of slash mostly did
The Trans-Catalina Trail.

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:30.750
What I did do was backpack
32 miles with a heavy pack

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.770
and camp out three nights.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:34.773
I feel ready for the apocalypse.

00:11:34.778 --> 00:11:36.918
Look, it's John!
- Hey, Ari.

00:11:36.918 --> 00:11:37.835
We made it.

00:11:37.924 --> 00:11:38.924
- [Ari] How'd it go?

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:39.983
- I feel great!

00:11:40.099 --> 00:11:44.690
Like, the sense of
self-satisfaction, it's...

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.220
- I had a lot of time
to reflect on my hike,

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.023
and I feel much more at ease.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:53.590
So, what is even the point of
walking for miles and miles

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:54.723
with a heavy backpack?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:59.280
For me, it's doing something
difficult on my own terms

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:02.490
so that when life gets
difficult, which it does,

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.000
I know that I have that
strength to call on

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.943
to endure and persevere.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:09.323
This is my final waste from my trip,

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:12.203
and we have to throw
away these sardine cans.

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.323
These apple cores and
teabags I'm gonna compost,

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:17.563
and this still has a lot of uses in it.

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.310
Unfortunately, this is all the trash

00:12:19.310 --> 00:12:22.260
from the gear that I got, but
I am going to recycle it all.

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.730
I'm laughing a little bit at
my sob session I had yesterday

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:28.483
at the beauty of the
trail, but you know what?

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:32.270
You can take drugs and get
that feeling a lot quicker

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.640
or you could try backpacking.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:34.473
I brought tee-pee,

00:12:34.473 --> 00:12:35.530
but I haven't used any

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:37.740
because I've been air
drying along the trail,

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:39.142
and I've been doing more serious things

00:12:39.142 --> 00:12:40.953
at the campsite bathrooms.

